{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkiWjj6YmPsDK8aGdxhh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F7RGwFb8RYW9GoRudqJcL5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-171824__x10629c/work/CreditorCreek-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-171824; sed -n 2762,2830p kit/API.md; grep -n \"interface SpriteOptions\" -A12 kit/API.md | head -30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1366,"cache_read_input_tokens":122933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1366},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"21fc944b-a909-4803-981c-3b41e54cde9f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:19:50.749Z","request_id":"req_011CgkiWjTjPxnrD2z9SWLow","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01F7RGwFb8RYW9GoRudqJcL5":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-171824__x10629c/work/CreditorCreek-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-171824; sed -n 2762,2830p kit/API.md; grep -n \"interface SpriteOptions\" -A12 kit/API.md | head -30"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F7RGwFb8RYW9GoRudqJcL5","type":"tool_result","content":"### class Hud\n\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n\n  ctx.hud.clear();\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n- `visible: boolean`\n- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n- `get height: number`\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### type HudAnchor\n\n```ts\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\n```\n\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\n\n### type HudColor\n\n```ts\ntype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\n```\n\n### interface HudOptions\n\n- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\n- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\n- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\n- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\n\n### hudPlace()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\n```\n\nTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n\n## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n\n### addModelColliders()\n\n```ts\nfunction addModelColliders(physics: Physics, build: Pick<ModelBuild, 'colliders'>, at: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0], yaw = 0): RAPIER.Collider[]\n```\n\nStatic Rapier colliders for a placed model (its `colliders` data), at `at` turned `yaw`\nradians about Y: a box, an upright cylinder or a convex hull, with `addStaticBox`'s friction.\n\n4791:### interface SpriteOptions\n4792-\n4793-- `size?: number`: Height in metres (the width follows the frame's aspect). Default 1.\n4794-- `frame?: number`\n4795-- `flip?: boolean`: Mirror left-right (a sprite facing the other way).\n4796-\n4797-### interface SpriteSheet\n4798-\n4799-- `readonly texture: Texture`: The sheet (nearest-filtered); `drawSheet` makes one from code. Frames run left to right, top to bottom, from the image's top-left; a texture with `flipY` false (a `DataTexture`) holds its rows top line first.\n4800-- `readonly frame: readonly [number, number]`: Frame size in pixels and the frames across and down.\n4801-- `readonly cols: number`\n4802-- `readonly rows: number`\n4803-- `readonly frames: number`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"1471f3bc-9a90-4f02-8e0d-595bfefc7b3b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:19:50.769Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### class Hud\n\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n\n  ctx.hud.clear();\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n- `visible: boolean`\n- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n- `get height: number`\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### type HudAnchor\n\n```ts\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\n```\n\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\n\n### type HudColor\n\n```ts\ntype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\n```\n\n### interface HudOptions\n\n- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\n- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\n- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\n- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\n\n### hudPlace()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\n```\n\nTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n\n## 11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n\n### addModelColliders()\n\n```ts\nfunction addModelColliders(physics: Physics, build: Pick<ModelBuild, 'colliders'>, at: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0], yaw = 0): RAPIER.Collider[]\n```\n\nStatic Rapier colliders for a placed model (its `colliders` data), at `at` turned `yaw`\nradians about Y: a box, an upright cylinder or a convex hull, with `addStaticBox`'s friction.\n\n4791:### interface SpriteOptions\n4792-\n4793-- `size?: number`: Height in metres (the width follows the frame's aspect). Default 1.\n4794-- `frame?: number`\n4795-- `flip?: boolean`: Mirror left-right (a sprite facing the other way).\n4796-\n4797-### interface SpriteSheet\n4798-\n4799-- `readonly texture: Texture`: The sheet (nearest-filtered); `drawSheet` makes one from code. Frames run left to right, top to bottom, from the image's top-left; a texture with `flipY` false (a `DataTexture`) holds its rows top line first.\n4800-- `readonly frame: readonly [number, number]`: Frame size in pixels and the frames across and down.\n4801-- `readonly cols: number`\n4802-- `readonly rows: number`\n4803-- `readonly frames: number`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F7RGwFb8RYW9GoRudqJcL5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
