{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G7XsMsbS3T6sat2E2dLRqd","type":"tool_result","content":"`fixed` config into your game.\n\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane)\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts-17- * one collider per block. Merged meshes are culled as a whole, so merge things that are\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts-18- * on screen together (a level, a room), and keep anything that moves separate.\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts-19- */\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts:20:export declare function mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options?: MergeOptions): Mesh[];","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"f1a634c1-f00e-40e0-8c92-57b040496db5","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:47:31.400Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"`fixed` config into your game.\n\n### class CameraRig\n\nBase rig: owns the three.js camera, zoom and the ground-plane movement basis.\n\n- `new CameraRig(config: CameraConfig)`\n- `readonly preset: CameraPreset`\n- `readonly camera: OrthographicCamera | PerspectiveCamera`\n- `readonly focus: Vector3`: World point the rig is centred on (used for shadow framing).\n- `zoom: number`\n- `readonly minZoom: number`\n- `readonly maxZoom: number`\n- `readonly zoomable: boolean`: Whether zoom applies (all presets except first person).\n- `readonly hidesTarget: boolean`: First person hides the player model.\n- `readonly lockDepth: boolean`: Side-scroller: characters should stay on their depth lane.\n- `controlsCharacter: boolean`: False while the free camera is flying (input drives the camera, not the player).\n- `snap: boolean`: Pixel-snap the camera (ortho only).\n- `aspect: number`: Viewport aspect (width / height), following the art resolution (see `setAspect`).\n- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane)\n- `setZoom(zoom: number): void`\n- `setAspect(aspect: number): void`: Match the art resolution's aspect (adaptive framing changes it with the screen). `update()` calls this from `CameraUpdate.resolution`; the engine also calls it on swap.\n- `teleport(target: Vector3): void`: Place the camera without smoothing.\n- `groundBasis(): { right: Vector3; forward: Vector3 }`: Screen-relative movement basis on the ground plane.\n- `update(u: CameraUpdate): void`\n- `describe(): Record<string, unknown>`: Serializable description (debug UI, `state()`).\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts-17- * one collider per block. Merged meshes are culled as a whole, so merge things that are\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts-18- * on screen together (a level, a room), and keep anything that moves separate.\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts-19- */\nkit/types/engine/render/merge.d.ts:20:export declare function mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options?: MergeOptions): Mesh[];","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G7XsMsbS3T6sat2E2dLRqd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
