{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgknVUw3okiE1aPCGVTor","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built **Creditor Creek**, a playable life-sim vertical slice, but only part of PLAN.md. The full test run gives 400 checks, 0 failures, but the plan asked for more than I built, and the cuts are listed below.\n\n**How it plays.** You step off the last bus and owe Mrs. Gander, a goose, 8,000 beans. You work off the debt by catching fish and bugs, digging fossils, and selling to her. You also befriend eight odd neighbours and ride the bus to a neon City.\n\n**What's in it:**\n- **Village and neighbours:** a 60×46 village that keeps time, with weather and seasons across a 16-day year. The neighbours have routines and remember what you did.\n- **Day One:** the new-arrival bus conversation and the seven errands.\n- **City:** seven venues plus a fortune-teller's tent. The bus ride has a sung ballad built from your recent life.\n- **Year events:** four festivals, three contests, Vesper's show nights, the cheese market, Rocco leaving and Fitch moving in, Inspector Pimm, and the Long Night ending that rolls into Year Two.\n- **Shell:** title, settings with the 10% music default, pause menu, and a dev mode whose Balance page has 23 live sliders with per-slider and Reset All. Attract mode starts after 10 seconds idle and any input exits it. About/Credits and a touch-only notice are in too.\n- **Online:** the AI Hub round, \"The Bean Bazaar\", with its own card, passes all four harness scenarios.\n\n**Cuts and shortfalls** (not hidden in the game):\n- **Visit mode and WebRTC invite codes are not built.** I removed the Visit entry from the title.\n- **Left out of the plan:** dust bunnies, neighbour chat bubbles, the catalogue reorder, patterns on shirts and umbrellas, home tiers beyond a size change, and the two-storey home.\n- **Village size:** 60×46 instead of the plan's 80×64.\n- **Sheets check:** not run, because my art is built from primitives in code rather than the engine's model format.\n- **Not seen:** I checked screenshots of the title, village, dialogue, winter, City night, store, home, pockets, map, almanac, dev and About screens. I never looked at a festival, contest or attract mode picture. Those were covered by scripts only.\n\n**Delivered, in the work folder:**\n- `CreditorCreek-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-171824.html` (6.3 MB, opens from `file://`)\n- `exit-interview.json`, which parses\n- the dev folder `CreditorCreek-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-171824/`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n\nRun all tests with `node tests/run.mjs` from the dev folder.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 17:18:24\n- **Source:** Animal Crossing: City Folk\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** life sim / social sim; isometric 3/4 orthographic diorama camera (iso preset, 90° turns); same camera indoors as a dollhouse cutaway\n- **Tech:** Riftlight Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186 WebGPU, Rapier idle), esbuild 0.28 bundle, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native 3D-as-pixel-art in the 16-colour palette; own critter generator, buildings and quiet ground textures\n- **Animation:** engine ClipDef clips at 30 fps, compiled with `compileClips` onto a 7-joint rig and played with `THREE.AnimationMixer`; 44 clips\n- **Audio:** all in code: Song-sequencer music (hourly tunes, venues, festivals), SoundDef effects, Animalese-style formant voices; music defaults to 10%\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world round with its own card, passing the harness; no other network features\n- **Testing:** headless scripts only: simulation, a scripted whole-game playthrough on `Engine.headless`, Chromium on `file://` with software WebGPU (boot, input, attract, audio, phone and tablet profiles), a WebKit failure-message check, and the AI Hub harness (4 scenarios); no subagents\n- **Research:** read PLAN.md, the engine guide and API docs, and the AI Hub README; no web research\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 14 real ones:\n  - a boot-order crash;\n  - the player never drawn;\n  - a dead tool button;\n  - saplings that never grew;\n  - attract mode deadlocked;\n  - the pause menu reopening the instant it closed;\n  - Continue also pressing the bus stop;\n  - rain and snow showing in sunshine;\n  - voice syllables clipping at 1.0;\n  - digging refused on plaza tiles;\n  - a Pimm visit blocking a test;\n  - a few mistakes in my own test code.\n- **How many were critical or game-breaking?** Five: the boot-order crash, the invisible player, the dead tool button, the attract deadlock and the pause reopen loop.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough on `Engine.headless`. It drives real input through arrival, errands, tools, shop, museum, home, every venue, cheese, Vesper, all festivals and contests, Rocco, bed, seasons, absence, Pimm and the ending in about a minute, and says exactly where it broke.\n- **Least helpful test:** the WebKit no-WebGPU check and the dialogue-line counts, which pass trivially. The sheets check doesn't apply to this art.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** one shared look. Toon bands, outlines and the 16-colour palette make code-built boxes read as intentional art, and the same game runs headless in Node.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes: `ctx.random.fork()` returns an object, not a function; `NavGrid`'s origin is the corner of cell (0,0); manual `step()` loops starve promises unless you yield; `Precipitation` needs `intensity` 0 as well as `visible=false`; and the Euler signs on a custom rig took a few renders to confirm.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the whole interface layer (bitmap font, panels, focus and pointer hit-testing, glyph prompts, dialogue, all the screens), then the critter generator and the data-driven rooms.\n- **Hardest part:** mapping the pointer onto HUD pixels under the fixed-aspect letterbox, and drawing lots of mixed-case text cheaply.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none. `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the kit, and a test asserts it.\n- **One change I'd ask for:** an awaitable `engine.stepAsync(n)`, plus a callable `ctx.random`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the verified recipes (the browser-flags correction, the pause rule, the music-volume arithmetic) and the pillars that justified each cut.\n- **Confusing:** squaring \"feature-complete, nothing left half-built\" with a plan far larger than one session; the cut rules say what never to cut but not how big each system should be. Also whether the deliverable name keeps the spaces of the title and source (I removed them).\n- **Hardest:** choosing scope. Each venue, festival and contest deserved a week; finding a real, hands-on, small version of each was the work.\n- **Would change:** give each section a size budget and a ranked minimal slice, say which cross-checks matter most, and state whether Visit may be dropped when only one transport is built."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1411,"cache_read_input_tokens":564627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1411},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"145d281e-cab4-4a6b-b690-e45af10cb458","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:12:17.926Z","request_id":"req_011CgknVUTH663ioF3UfjVKz"}
