{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkoEmpFqLTnun3qgHBzC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback answers are now updated to match what I actually built, and I looked at screenshots of the annex and the Lost & Found bin. I did not find anything new in PLAN.md to build this round, and I ran only the browser suite after the last rebuild (41 checks, 0 failures); the full run last passed at 422.\n\n- **Annex:** I put a couch and a lamp in it and the screenshot shows both inside the room with no problems.\n- **Lost & Found:** the screenshot shows Clementine's opening line (\"The bin holds 2 things…\") when you open the bin. I did not look at the list of items you take from, which is the same screen widget the catalogue uses.\n- **Feedback answers:** the Testing answers now say about 18 issues, include the later ones found from screenshots, and report the final 422 checks. The sheets check now reads as passing but covering only three props, so it says little. The prompt answer now says I built the two-window Visit, not invite codes.\n\n`exit-interview.json`, the About screen text and the built HTML in the work folder all carry the updated answers.\n\nStill not done from PLAN.md:\n- WebRTC invite codes for Visit between two computers.\n- Most of the art is built from primitives in code rather than the engine's model format, so the sheets check covers little of it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1005,"cache_read_input_tokens":604987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1005},"output_tokens":429,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"5edb117