{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkpfGAMMzf9gmjTQ8xr2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full test run is still going, so I can't yet say it passes on the final build. I'll report the result when it finishes.\n\nWhat changed this round:\n\n- **Silhouettes:** I lined up the species in the village and looked at screenshots of 14 of the 27. The moose with antlers and laundry, platypus with its bill, lemur with its ringed tail, yak, goose, capybara with its bee, snail, pangolin and moth are all clearly distinct. The wombat and quokka are the closest pair and read as similar rounded blobs. I did not look at the other 13 species.\n- **Magda's forgery display:** her shop now hangs the painting model on the wall and the camera pulls in to show it. The screenshot shows a framed Whistler's Moose. I did not check how a forgery's red mark looks on it.\n- **Dr. Quill:** he rolls into a ball for about 2.4 seconds when you donate. While doing this I found that host characters inside interiors weren't being animated at all. They are now, so every host character plays its idle clip.\n- **Hats and glasses:** the clothes lists now meet the plan's floors: 24 outfits, 12 hats, 6 glasses and 6 umbrellas. Hats, glasses and umbrellas take their colour from the item data.\n- **Lost & Found:** I looked at the list screen. It shows the three items, their descriptions and the Take prompt.\n- **Annex:** I looked at the annex earlier this session and it showed furniture correctly.\n\nI updated `exit-interview.json` before this test run started, but the About and feedback text haven't been rechecked against the new clothes counts."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":451,"cache_read_input_tokens":685669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":451},"output_tokens":529,"service_tier":"st