{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkqU4wjXSWDsuJpMgGjD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Visit now passes between two separate browser processes too: 15 checks, 0 failures.\n\nThe last item, Visit on two real computers, is the only one open, and I can't do it on this computer. There is no second machine here.\n\nI tested the Gate Pass and Reply Slip exchange in three ways:\n- Between two pages in one browser session (BroadcastChannel).\n- Between two pages in separate browser sessions of the same browser.\n- Between two completely separate browser processes (new this round), where the guest arrives in the host's town and movement shows up on the host.\n\nAll three run with no ICE servers, so they exercise the same WebRTC code as a two-computer connection; what they don't test is real network traffic. TASK.md says to play multiplayer with two browser pages on this computer when there is no second player, and these tests do that.\n\nThe full suite last passed at 426 checks before I added the new Visit checks; I ran only the Visit test this round. `exit-interview.json`, the built HTML, the dev folder and `PROGRESS.md` are in the work folder and unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":717600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400},"output_tokens":342,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"53762218-f923-4930-b241-7e01cdc4d747","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:51:05.769Z","request_id":"req_011CgkqU4NkJkGEZ9qKHt2dz"}
