{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QpvqWaEPHJmYvMxMkefLq1","type":"tool_result","content":"### class RenderView\n\n- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `enabled: boolean`\n- `get texture: Texture`\n- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface RenderViewOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n- `near?: number`\n- `far?: number`\n- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n\n### class Rng\n### class Mirror\n\n- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `width` x `height`, the art resolution). Skipped when the camera is be\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs (nothing is drawn).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface MirrorOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Width and height of the glass (m). Default [4, 2].\n- `tint?: number`: A colour the reflection leans toward, and how much (0..1). Default a faint blue, 0.15.\n- `tintAmount?: number`\n4323:### groundFog()\n4324-\n4325-```ts\n4326-function groundFog(o: { color?: number; top?: number; amount?: number; near?: number; far?: number } = {}): { node: Node; color: UniformNode<\"color\", Color>; amount: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; top: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; }\n4327-```\n4328-\n4329-Fog for `scene.fogNode` with live settings (uniforms: changing them never recompiles):\n4330-ground mist that thickens below `top` (m) and a haze that grows with distance from the\n4331-camera, both up to `amount` (0..1), in `color` (match the sky).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"541dfb74-6d26-4eed-a3fa-1afc1c236b36","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:57:37.974Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### class RenderView\n\n- `new RenderView(o: RenderViewOptions = {})`\n- `static screen(object: Object3D): void`: Put `object` (and its children) on the screens' layer.\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `readonly camera: PerspectiveCamera`\n- `every: number`: Render every nth frame.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `enabled: boolean`\n- `get texture: Texture`\n- `setSize(w: number, h: number): void`: Resize the texture (the camera's aspect follows).\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene): boolean`: Draw `scene` from the view's camera into its texture, if this is one of its frames. True if it drew.\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`). Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs.\n- `screenMaterial(): MeshBasicNodeMaterial`: An unlit material showing the view (a new one each call: tint it as you like).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface RenderViewOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Texture size in pixels (default [160, 90]).\n- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view, degrees (default 60).\n- `near?: number`\n- `far?: number`\n- `every?: number`: Render every nth frame (default 1): a slow refresh costs less.\n\n### class Rng\n### class Mirror\n\n- `new Mirror(o: MirrorOptions = {})`\n- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n- `readonly target: RenderTarget`\n- `enabled: boolean`: False: the glass shows plain glass and nothing is rendered for it.\n- `renders: number`: Times it has rendered.\n- `render(renderer: WebGPURenderer, scene: Scene, camera: Camera, width: number, height: number): boolean`: Reflect `camera` in the glass and draw `scene` from there into the texture (sized `width` x `height`, the art resolution). Skipped when the camera is be\n- `attach(view: View, scene: Scene): () => void`: Render before every frame of `view` (`engine.renderer`), from its camera, at its art size. Returns a stop. Headless the hook is kept and never runs (nothing is drawn).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface MirrorOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Width and height of the glass (m). Default [4, 2].\n- `tint?: number`: A colour the reflection leans toward, and how much (0..1). Default a faint blue, 0.15.\n- `tintAmount?: number`\n4323:### groundFog()\n4324-\n4325-```ts\n4326-function groundFog(o: { color?: number; top?: number; amount?: number; near?: number; far?: number } = {}): { node: Node; color: UniformNode<\"color\", Color>; amount: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; top: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; }\n4327-```\n4328-\n4329-Fog for `scene.fogNode` with live settings (uniforms: changing them never recompiles):\n4330-ground mist that thickens below `top` (m) and a haze that grows with distance from the\n4331-camera, both up to `amount` (0..1), in