{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgktFNRSUXWJzeMNJFx5s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full suite had two failures in the two-session Visit test: the guest was still on the title screen when the test checked. I re-ran the Visit test five times and it passed every time, so I treat it as a timing flake, not a real fault. It only showed up under load with the whole suite running, which is the same kind of flake I saw earlier in the AI Hub harness.\n\nI made the test more patient: both connection waits now allow up to 150 rounds of frames, not 40. This changes only the test, not the game. I have not re-run the whole suite since this change, so I can't yet show a clean full run. The last complete full run was 444 checks, 0 failures, before the festival changes. The rest of that run (simulation, playthrough, browser, hub, sheets) passed with the festival changes in place; only the Visit WebRTC checks failed.\n\nThe built HTML, `exit-interview.json`, the dev folder with `AUDIT.md`, and `PROGRESS.md` are in the work folder. The remaining gaps are unchanged: Visit on two real computers (no second machine here), the festivals still being compact set pieces, and the tail motion, ambience, cloud shadows, gold Bell and festival animations not seen or heard by me."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":829887,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":393},"output_tokens":392,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"a9717091-5b77-4d88-8d3c-329e5f845c39","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:27:34.460Z","request_id":"req_011CgktFN3N3eFFBExddt79F"}
