{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"bqubthxm1","run_id":"0mw4dh3ss-c523ca9d","tool_use_id":"toolu_011hhGUjVmtKxiBsGxLJW1xU","status":"completed","output_file":"","summary":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-171824__x10629c/work/CreditorCreek*/; python3 - <<'E'\np='tests/play/playthrough.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"// settings, 10% music default\",\"\"\"// Day 10 mushrooms, moving boxes, frosted windows, snow footprints\nw.day = 10; w.movedOut.rocco = false; sys.nature.daily(g); T.ok(w.town.items.some(i => i.id === 'mushroom' && i.wild), 'mushrooms grow at the woods\\\\' edge in autumn'); w.day = 8; g.syncAll(); T.ok(g.town.extras.length >= 1 && g.town.buildings.get('rocco').children.some(c => c.children.length >= 6), 'moving boxes appear at Rocco\\\\'s door'); w.day = 14; g.syncAll(); { const b = g.town.buildings.get('dorrit'); T.ok(b.userData.glass[0].material.color.getHex() === (await import('../../src/pixel-engine.js')).PALETTE.white, 'windows frost over in winter'); }\ng.place = 'town'; g.player.pos.x = 12; g.player.pos.z = 31; g.footstep(g.player.pos, 'walk'); T.ok(g.prints?.list.length >= 1, 'snow footprints appear on winter grass');\n// settings, 10% music default\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nnode tests/run.mjs --only play | tail -3; cd ..; awk 'NR>=600 && NR<=700' PLAN.md | grep -E \"^\\*\\*|^- |^\\| \" | cut -c1-330 | head -40","uuid":"bad94deb-b86b-4556-8912-7e680c030016","session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011hhGUjVmtKxiBsGxLJW1xU","type":"tool_result","content":"FAIL play: no summary\n[play] TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '0')\n0 checks, 1 failures (play)\n**Base style:** the engine's native 3D-as-pixel-art with the default look (`LOOK_PRESETS.none`): toon bands, pixel outlines, Sweetie 16. Rendered comparisons: `none` and `pixel_world` read best, `dream` blooms too much, `cel_cartoon` stops feeling like pixel art. Use `none`.\n**Readability rules.** Quiet ground, loud actors. Dark outlines. Chunky shapes (≥ 0.25 m, per the guide). Doors, windows and signs are the most saturated things on a building. Reference proportions [verified]: cottage walls 4.4×2.2×3.6 m with two wedge roofs and a chimney; critters 1.5 m with a 0.9 m head; `lamp-post`, `notice-b\n**New assets to make (they're what makes it feel like this game):**\n- **Critter generator** (`src/art/critter.js`): parts for head shape, ears, antlers, bills, tails, shell, hair, clothes, from one function. All neighbours, hosts and crowd come from it. Each needs a distinct silhouette at 45 px: moose antlers with laundry, platypus bill and tiara, armadillo bands, lemur ringed tail (`SpringChain\n- **Buildings:** home ×4 tiers, store ×3, Town Hall with Post flag, Museum with columns, Mothwick's with giant spool, 9 cottages (shared shell, personal decoration), bus and shelter, 8 City fronts with neon, City skyline, lighthouse.\n- **Nature:** own trees (pear, pine, palm, plus stages) with seasonal palettes and fruit, flowers (4 species), weeds, saplings, beanstalk, Old Pear (huge), Old Bell, river banks, cliffs, ramps, bridges.\n- **Items:** tools; fish and bugs (parametric: body, fins, colour; library `butterfly`/`firefly` sprites are fine for flyers); fossils; 8 paintings (pixel `TextureDef`s with a forgery variant); hats; furniture signature pieces; cheese wheel; snowman; lanterns; balloon.\n**Life everywhere.** Blinking, tails, smoke, swaying crowns, cloud shadows, birds (`Boids`), fish rings, laundry, butterflies, puddles, petals, leaves, lit windows. If a screen is ever still for 3 seconds, something's missing. Performance is out of scope: add what the scene needs.\n**Every sheet goes through** `node check.mjs --sheets` from your kit (exit 0, no problems; warnings fixed unless you mean them). **Look at the PNGs in the game too.**\n**System:** the engine's clip format (`ClipDef` data at 30 fps, full poses, easing, sine layers), compiled with `compileClips` onto the 7-joint rig, played with `THREE.AnimationMixer`, cross-faded with `crossFadeTo`. Plus `Squash` (stop, land, pick up), `SpringChain` (tails, ears, ribbons), code-driven face parts, and head turns\n**Clips (floor 30):** Idle, IdleBored, Walk, Jog, Run, Tiptoe, Talk, Listen, Nod, ShakeHead, Laugh, Cry, Shock, Anger, Love, Shrug, Bow, Dance, Wave, Sit, Sleep, PlayDead, HoldUp, PickUp, Give, NetReady, NetSweep, Cast, Reel, Dig, Chop, Water, ShakeTree, Slingshot, PushSnow, Eat, Hum, Sway, Sting, Slip, plus species specials: Ma\n**Feel notes.** Net: 3 frames of anticipation then a fast arc. Tree shake: canopy wobble and leaves. Dig: three dirt chunks, then a hole. Bite: bobber snaps under. HoldUp: both arms, item above head, pause. Dialogue: small nods and talk mouth on syllables. `validateClip(clip, RIG)` returns nothing in tests; check `renderSheet` c\n**Music volume defaults to 10%.** The engine's default is 60%, stored under `pixel-engine:audio`. On a profile with no stored audio, call `audio.setVolume('music', 0.1)` before any music starts. **Author tracks hot**: make simultaneous track volumes sum to about 1.0 [verified numbers, section 2], or 10% is inaudible. Settings Re\n**Music** (all new; easygoing, a little jazzy, lots of walking bass; `stepsPerBeat: 3` gives a swing feel):\n| Set | Count (floor → target) |\n| **Hourly tunes:** every one of the 24 hours has its own arrangement, each with rain and snow variants, built by `composer.js` from hand-written motifs (transposition, tempo, re-voicing) | 8 → 12 motifs |\n| Title, credits, bus ride, bed lullaby | 4 |\n| Venues: store, museum, Mothwick's, Hall, City day, City night, salon, couture, Magda's, theatre, auction, café, Bureau | 13 |\n| Festivals, contests, season stings | 4 + 1 + 4 |\n| Vesper's records | 6 |\n**Ambience** with `audio.loop` voices and `spatialize`: river, surf, rain, wind, crickets, birds, City hum, neon buzz.\n**Effects** (floor 40): footsteps per surface, each tool, splashes, bite, pick-ups, reveal jingle, UI tick, confirm, cancel, doors, mail flag, bus engine, HONK, paddle, cheese smell, firework.\n**Voices: gibberish, Animalese/Simlish style, code only** [method verified]. Each letter of the typed line triggers a very short syllable: a `SoundDef` of stacked sine harmonics whose weights follow vowel formants (a harmonic stack through `layers`), with noise layers for consonants.\n**The round.** Five minutes on a 32×24 Fair Green (pond and river strip, small orchard, flower patch, dig cracks, a central stall), in the village's art.\n- All verbs are contextual on one button, no tool switching: shake, dig, cast, reel, swing, sell.\n- Five pocket slots. Unbanked value counts half at the bell, so trips to the stall matter.\n- Neighbours post short orders (\"Dorrit wants a pear: double beans\").\n- A bell announces golden moments (golden fish, a rich tree) at set times. The Mayor inches across the green; bump him for a tip of the sash and small bonus.\n- Avatars wear seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`) with hub names over their heads (never inserted as HTML). A scoreboard strip shows everyone.\n**Own card** (`connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true })`): the plaza, players lined up in their colours, the game's name, who's ready, how to win, this player's controls, time left from the `card` event. Answers: Ready = Enter, Cross or click, `AIHub.answer('ready')`; More time = Triangle, a named key or click, `\n**Protocol duties.**\n- Play starts at `AIHub.time() >= 0`; show the 3-second countdown from `start`.\n- Host is authoritative. Bell at min(5:00, `limitMs` − 5 s): `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` listing every player still in `AIHub.players`, ties grouped. Comic awards (\"Most Fish Apologised To\").\n- On `time-up`, finish at once.\n- On `leave`, remove the avatar.\n- On `end`, stop input, `audio.stopMusic()` and `stopLoops()`, send nothing.\n- `server` copy: `AIHub.server` true, no local player, input or avatar; slow overview camera; runs the world as usual.\n- Use `AIHub.rng(label)` for host-independent randomness.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"1aeb4a15-a83a-4a29-b2ff-7731d5cadb81","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:45:47.715Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FAIL play: no summary\n[play] TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '0')\n0 checks, 1 failures (play)\n**Base style:** the engine's native 3D-as-pixel-art with the default look (`LOOK_PRESETS.none`): toon bands, pixel outlines, Sweetie 16. Rendered comparisons: `none` and `pixel_world` read best, `dream` blooms too much, `cel_cartoon` stops feeling like pixel art. Use `none`.\n**Readability rules.** Quiet ground, loud actors. Dark outlines. Chunky shapes (≥ 0.25 m, per the guide). Doors, windows and signs are the most saturated things on a building. Reference proportions [verified]: cottage walls 4.4×2.2×3.6 m with two wedge roofs and a chimney; critters 1.5 m with a 0.9 m head; `lamp-post`, `notice-b\n**New assets to make (they're what makes it feel like this game):**\n- **Critter generator** (`src/art/critter.js`): parts for head shape, ears, antlers, bills, tails, shell, hair, clothes, from one function. All neighbours, hosts and crowd come from it. Each needs a distinct silhouette at 45 px: moose antlers with laundry, platypus bill and tiara, armadillo bands, lemur ringed tail (`