{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkujYXnx87VRavtWMts3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full suite is running on the latest build, and I'll report when it finishes.\n\nThis round I fixed the four small items from the last hook feedback and then read sections 16 to 20 of the plan sentence by sentence.\n\n**The four items I named last time (all now tested):**\n- **Frosted windows:** windows turn white in winter. Cottages had no windows at all because the door left no room, so I gave them side windows first.\n- **Moving boxes:** crates appear at Rocco's door on days 7 and 8, before he leaves.\n- **Mushrooms:** from day 10 of autumn, mushrooms grow at the woods' edge.\n- **Snow footprints:** you leave alternating prints on winter grass.\n\n**Things the section 16 to 20 pass turned up:**\n- **Birds:** a flock of small birds flies over the village on fine days.\n- **Street musician:** one stands in the City and plays notes as you walk near.\n- **Mayor Trundle:** he slides instead of walking.\n- **Squash:** your avatar squashes slightly when picking something up.\n- **Mrs. Gander:** she honks whenever her line contains \"HONK\".\n- **Speech speed:** Pemberton talks at double speed and Lou at a crawl.\n- **Vesper:** she sings a short tune when you ask for a song.\n\nThe play suite is now 123 checks, 0 failures; I'll know the full total when the run finishes. I haven't looked at the birds, musician, footprints or boxes on screen.\n\nStill not matched, per `AUDIT.md`: the Mayor's arrival scripting beyond the Seed Toss ribbon, fish rings on the water, and a highlight on the target tile. I haven't read sections 21 to 24 sentence by sentence. Visit on two real computers is still untested because there is no second machine here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":895564,"