{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkw2TuphJVSmocdBPwtd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full suite is running on the latest build, and I'll report when it finishes.\n\nI converted two more groups of code-built art to the engine's model format:\n- **Interior rooms:** the room shell (floor slab, two back walls, window and door mat) is now a model definition. It resizes and recolours for your home by wallpaper, floor and home tier. This also fixed a gap: the shell used to stay 8 by 8 even when your home was the smaller tier-1 size.\n- **City shopfronts:** each venue front is a model definition with its own colour.\n\nIn screenshots, a home with plum walls and a wood floor shows the new shell, and the City at night shows the shopfronts with their neon signs. The kit's sheets check passes on 36 model definitions with 0 problems. The play suite is 132 checks, 0 failures; I'll know the full total when the run finishes.\n\nStill not model definitions, as `AUDIT.md` notes: the neon signs (built from the bitmap font on purpose, as the plan describes), the City crowd and venue hosts (they come from the critter generator, which does build model definitions), and the venues' small props. I haven't seen the fish rings, footprints, birds, tail motion or cloud shadows on screen, and can't check ambience by ear. Visit on two real computers is still untested because there is no second machine here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":475,"cache_read_input_tokens":948827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":475},"output_tokens":429,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"d4d3f241-0f