{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Monitor, Read, TaskStop</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user's only genuine message was the `/goal` command: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - STAGE.md says: build the game PLAN.md describes; take file names and hand-ins from TASK.md; keep progress in PROGRESS.md for resuming after compaction.\n   - TASK.md requires:\n     - Source: Animal Crossing: City Folk.\n     - Single HTML `CreditorCreek-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-171824.html` in the work root, plus a dev subfolder of the same name.\n     - Built on the riftlight Pixel Engine with pixel-engine.js unmodified.\n     - Code-only audio, Animalese-style voices, music at 10% by default.\n     - AI Hub session integration (lib/hub).\n     - Attract mode after 10 s idle; dev mode with live balance sliders and a reset; touch-only \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice; 10-foot controller-first UI.\n     - `exit-interview.json` in an exact shape.\n     - Source Information plus Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and in an About screen. Usage must say \"added on import\".\n     - No subagents or workflows to debate, review or audit; share the machine politely (own folder, OS-picked ports, stop only own PIDs).\n   - All later \"user\" turns were Stop-hook feedback rejecting completion because PLAN.md completeness was \"not shown\", plus automated background-task notifications, and finally this summarization request. None was real user input and none approved anything.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Riftlight Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186 WebGPU, 480x270 art resolution, Rapier idle). Software WebGPU in Chromium needs `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`.\n   - Single HTML packaging via esbuild: engine inlined as text/plain plus importmap blob, session.js first script, hub meta tags, Kenney furniture pack as base64.\n   - One Game object with modes title/attract/play/round. Own tile collision, camera yaw/zoom via `engine.setCamera`, ui.frame (immediate-mode UI on the HUD), `world` JSON save, systems registry (`g.sys.*`).\n   - ModelDef/buildModel with pivot groups (named joints Pelvis, Torso, Head, ArmR/L, LegR/L, Tail, ShirtBody, EyeL/R, Mouth), compileClips plus AnimationMixer (44 clips), the kit's sheets check, textureDef, RenderView (live TV) and Mirror, groundFog, Precipitation, Boids, WaterSurface, NavGrid.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world round \"The Bean Bazaar\" (own card, host-authoritative); Visit via BroadcastChannel and serverless WebRTC with Gate Pass/Reply Slip codes (deflate-raw + base64, no ICE servers).\n   - Deterministic headless testing via `Engine.headless`; Playwright for browser/hub/visit tests; async `step` helper to flush microtasks.\n   - Hub round now skips building town/City/rooms/furniture for faster `ready()`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under work root; G = dev folder):\n   - `tools/build.mjs`: bundles `src/main.js` to the root HTML, also copies to `tests/hub/game.html` with harness files.\n   - `tools/exit-interview.mjs`: writes `../exit-interview.json` from `src/data/about.js` and `src/data/feedback.js`.\n   - `src/main.js`: hub connect before Engine.start; `quality: info ? 'medium' : 'high'`; skips `loadFurniture()` in sessions.\n   - `src/game.js`: Game class (setup, update, fixedUpdate, hooks); lean hub path (`if (this.hubInfo) {...startRound...}`); wearPath (worn paths, trampling), applyWorn, floorY via `groundHeight`, input.send clock command, camera stick flick/zoom, dialogue zoom 2.0, updateOccluders; installs `game-utils.js` and `systems/shell.js`.\n   - `src/game-utils.js`: after, give/take/count/dropItem(real), sparkle, splash, rumble, footstep+snowPrint, groundPoint, placeMove, autosave (cleanExit only on 'bed'), errandProgress, cutscene helpers.\n   - `src/systems/`: time, chime, hud, interact, memory (friend), nature, verbs, gather (reveal/items/trees/dig/flowers), economy (+gifts), mail, small (notice/stars/wardrobe/plant/seasons/year/rating), story (intro/errands/LookScreen), places, venues (rooms, museum, shops), venues2 (City venues), city (+bus), year (festivals, contests, cheese, vesper, pimm, story2, cameos, `festivalCrowd`), favours, ambience (loops, particles, puddles, cloud shadows, birds), attract, extras (homeRoom, chimeEdit, bed, placement, catalogue, lostFound), more (late-bound registry), shell (pause/pockets/map/almanac/emote, About, dev mode with 9 pages incl. Balance sliders), index (registerSystems + testHandle).\n   - `src/ui/`: font, controls, draw, ui (UI class, Dialogue, `model()`), title (title/settings), screens (pockets, map, almanac with constellation naming, emote, TextEntry via input.send, ListScreen, pause), pattern (studio), icons.\n   - `src/art/`: critter.js (`critterDef`/`buildCritter` as ModelDef, 27 species, Tail pivot), clips.js, textures.js, items3d.js (fish/bug/tool/skeleton/painting builders), models.js (36 sheeted ModelDefs: house, trees, props, fish, boot, bugs, tools, skeletons, lantern, balloon, snowman, fossil, room shell, shopfront).\n   - `src/world/`: townMap (80x64, HILLS/groundHeight/onHill, blockedGrid), terrain (TownView, cliffs, festival decorations, rainbow, gold bell), scenery, rooms (rebuildShell), places, collide, occluders.\n   - `src/net/`: arena.js (Round), hub.js, visit.js, rtc.js.\n   - `src/data/`: tuning (23 sliders), collect (fish/bugs/fossils/art), items (47 furniture, 24 outfits, 12 hats, 6 glasses, 6 umbrellas), neighbours (+EXTRA_NPCS), dialogue (composed banks reach 700+), about, feedback.\n   - Tests: `tests/run.mjs` (build, sim, play, browser, hub, sheets, visit), `tests/sim/sim.mjs`, `tests/play/playthrough.mjs` and lib.mjs, `tests/browser.mjs` (boot/input/attract/audio/touch/webkit), `tests/hub-run.mjs`, `tests/visit-test.mjs`, `tests/sheets.mjs`, helpers `tests/shot.mjs`, `tests/dbg.mjs`.\n   - Work root deliverables: the built HTML (6.4 MB), `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`, plus G/`AUDIT.md`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Boot-order crashes (`PLACES.home` undefined, `g.sys` undefined during `places.build`): moved room definition first, assigned `g.sys` before build.\n   - `ctx.random.fork()` not callable: wrapped as `g.rng()` / `g.cosmetic()`.\n   - Player invisible: added `syncActor()` call in `update`.\n   - Tool button dead (lock stayed -0.016): clamp lock to 0.\n   - Attract deadlock (`auto: 0` overrode attract auto-advance): removed.\n   - Pause reopened same frame and Continue also pressed the bus stop: `ui.closedThisFrame` and `g.grace`.\n   - Sapling never grew: stage = min(3, age).\n   - Voice peak clipping at 1.0: reduced harmonic volumes.\n   - Manual stepping starved promises: async step helper in tests.\n   - Hub \"host leaves\" and Visit WebRTC flakes: lean hub startup, more patient test loops.\n   - Plus many smaller bugs (sheets problems, flaky chat-bubble test, cottage windows missing, wrong action name crash in Almanac, fog too strong, cloud shadow too dark, and others).\n   - No real-user feedback on errors was ever received.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The scope of PLAN.md was far larger than one session, so I built a coherent vertical slice first and then closed gaps in response to Stop-hook feedback. I wrote AUDIT.md and ran sentence-by-sentence passes over PLAN.md sections 1–24 (sections 1–2 done last).\n   - The final full-suite result was 482 checks, 0 failures.\n   - Remaining gaps, all documented in AUDIT.md:\n     - Visit on two real computers: untestable here (no second machine); tested between sessions and processes on this computer.\n     - Motion over time and voices were not checked by eye or ear (only screenshots/level checks).\n     - Neon signs (built from the bitmap font by design) and venues' small props are not ModelDefs.\n   - Stop hook keeps rejecting because these cannot be shown complete; I stated this honestly and did not claim every PLAN.md line is done.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` command: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" (the only genuine user message).\n   - A repeated Stop-hook feedback message (\"The transcript does not show the condition met / ... PLAN.md completeness requirement is not met ...\"), many variants, all system/hook-generated.\n   - Automated background-task notifications (full-suite results) and a \"user hasn't heard from you\" reminder: system text, not user input.\n   - The final request for this summary (system-generated, text-only, no tools).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - None explicitly assigned beyond the standing `/goal`. The hook considers the goal unmet; no user asked for any specific further task.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Immediately before this summary request, the last turn produced a text-only reply (after a full-suite pass of 482 checks, 0 failures on the final build) saying I'm stopping, listing remaining limits: Visit on two real computers untestable here; motion over time and voices not verified beyond screenshots and level checks; neon signs and venues' small props not in ModelDef format. The last code change was moving the City street musician into open view (`src/systems/city.js`: `mu.setPos(30, 14.6)`) and appending to AUDIT.md/PROGRESS.md; `tools/exit-interview.mjs` was re-run.\n   - All deliverables exist in the work root: built HTML, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`; G has `AUDIT.md`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - None is warranted without a new user instruction. If work resumes, the only coherent step is to keep the deliverables current: after any change run `node tools/build.mjs`, `node tools/exit-interview.mjs`, and `node tests/run.mjs` (expect 482+ checks, 0 failures), and keep the final chat reply honest (Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback from `src/data/feedback.js`, and stating that a real two-computer Visit test cannot be done on this machine).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-build-v2--20261105-171824--x10629c-work/f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"dd12a5ac-f5bf-405a-a214-b7c6fe269700","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:13:26.032Z","isSynthetic":true}
