{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkwu8MWTTgP8yJRf8mJr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Creditor Creek** is built and handed in. The full test suite ran 482 checks with 0 failures on the final build. Everything in PLAN.md that I could do on this computer is done, with three limits listed below.\n\n**Hand-in files, in the work root:**\n- `CreditorCreek-AnimalCrossingCityFolk-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-171824.html` (6.4 MB, single file, engine inlined unmodified)\n- The dev folder of the same name, which also holds `AUDIT.md`\n- `exit-interview.json` (checked: it parses)\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n\n**What it is:** a 3D life sim in a small town that you settle while paying off a house loan. It has a day/night year with seasons, villagers who remember you, fishing, bugs, digging, a museum, shops, a City trip, festivals, mail, and decorating your home. It has an attract mode after 10 seconds on the title screen, a dev mode with live balance sliders and a reset, and a \"Controller or keyboard required\" screen for touch-only devices. A shared-world round called \"The Bean Bazaar\" runs through AI Hub. Visit works between two players by BroadcastChannel and by pasted codes over WebRTC.\n\n**Source Information**\n- Date: 2026-11-05 17:18:24\n- Source: Animal Crossing: City Folk\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: life sim; third-person 3D with a rotatable, zoomable camera\n- Tech: riftlight Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186 WebGPU), esbuild bundling, AI Hub lib/hub session protocol v1\n- Art Direction: the engine's native low-poly pixel style, with new models for the critters, buildings, furniture, fish, bugs and tools\n- Animation: the engine's model and clip system, with 44 new clips\n- Audio: all synthesized in code; Animalese-style gibberish voices; music at 10% by default\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world round, plus Visit through BroadcastChannel and WebRTC\n- Testing: headless engine runs, a scripted full playthrough, Playwright browser, hub and visit tests, a model-sheet check, and emulated controller and touch input\n- Research: none beyond the engine docs and the Hub library\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: added on import\n\n**Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback:** the full answers are in `exit-interview.json` and on the in-game About screen.\n\n**Not done or not verified:**\n- **Visit on two real computers:** there is no second machine here. I tested it between two pages and processes on this computer.\n- **Motion and voices:** I checked screenshots and audio levels, but not how the movement looks over time or how the voices sound.\n- **Neon signs and small venue props:** the signs are drawn from the bitmap font, and the smaller venue props still aren't engine ModelDefs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":31792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":455},"output_tokens":779,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f7fc0c99-6050-4a36-bbad-13de512b63e9","uuid":"8fd6ac9c-08e0-4eaf-a7a7-e1c2acabbf63","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:15:28.692Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkwu87d6zQR7ntQU2wrp"}
